@prefix lgo:  <https://legalgraph.org/ontology#> .
@prefix lgv:  <https://legalgraph.org/vocab/> .
@prefix lg:  <https://legalgraph.org/id/> .
@prefix eli:  <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Sweden: § 8 of the e-commerce act (SFS 2002:562) (additions to data/extracted/se/).

lg:SE-SFS-2002-562
    eli:title "Act on Electronic Commerce and Other Information Society Services"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "e-handelslagen" ;
    eli:id_local "SFS 2002:562" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2000-31 ;
    rdfs:comment "8 § asks for the organisationsnummer rather than a named register and adds nothing beyond the Directive's floor; the availability sentence and the lag 2025:989 broadcasting carve-out are separate unnumbered paragraphs."@en .


lg:SE-ABL
    lgo:shortName "ABL" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2017-1132 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.riksdagen.se/sv/dokument-och-lagar/dokument/svensk-forfattningssamling/aktiebolagslag-2005551_sfs-2005-551/> ;
    rdfs:comment "28 kap. 5 § is the Swedish company-law website duty: företagsnamn, styrelsens säte and organisationsnummer on brev, fakturor, orderblanketter och webbplatser, plus the liquidation fact. Andra stycket is the Bolagsverket dispensation to withhold the name and show company type instead."@en .

lg:SE-ARL
    lgo:shortName "ARL" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2013-11 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.riksdagen.se/sv/dokument-och-lagar/dokument/svensk-forfattningssamling/lag-2015671-om-alternativ-tvistlosning-i-konsument_sfs-2015-671/> ;
    rdfs:comment "10 § requires a trader committed to ADR to name the ADR board with its web and postal address on consumer-facing websites and in contract terms; 11 § is the durable-medium pointer when a consumer claim is rejected; 12 § points to art. 14 of the EU ODR regulation."@en .
